umiproc patch 0007: the first relocalized keyframe starts from the map's IMU bias, not zero

What: Tracking::Track, INIT_RELOCALIZE. While a run against a loaded map has no keyframe of its own yet
(mpLastKeyFrame is null, i.e. until its first relocalization), each frame waiting to relocalize gets the IMU bias
of the map's last keyframe (highest id: the keyframe the relocalized one is linked to as mPrevKF). On success the
new keyframe copies it, and patch 0003's fresh preintegration starts from it.
Why: only Track's "bias of the last keyframe" step sets a frame's bias, and before the first relocalization
there is no last keyframe, so the frame and the relocalized keyframe had a zero bias, the IMU was integrated
against zero bias, and (with no edge to the previous keyframe, patch 0003) nothing pulled it to the map's
estimate. Later relocalizations already carry the run's last keyframe's bias.
Behaviour change: localization runs (loaded map), from the first relocalization on: bias, IMU prediction and
preintegration start from the map's bias. No change in mapping runs.

diff --git a/src/Tracking.cc b/src/Tracking.cc
index 6da1bc1..baba67a 100644
--- a/src/Tracking.cc
+++ b/src/Tracking.cc
@@ -1660,6 +1660,17 @@ void Tracking::Track()
                 }
                 else if (mState == INIT_RELOCALIZE)
                 {
+                    // umiproc patch 0007: before the first relocalization of a run against a loaded map there is no
+                    // keyframe of this run, so the frame (and the keyframe made from it on success) kept a zero IMU
+                    // bias, and nothing ties it to the map's. Start from the bias of the map's last keyframe (the one
+                    // the relocalized keyframe is linked to). Later relocalizations already carry the bias of the
+                    // run's last keyframe (set at the top of Track).
+                    if(!mpLastKeyFrame && (mSensor==System::IMU_MONOCULAR || mSensor==System::IMU_STEREO || mSensor==System::IMU_RGBD))
+                    {
+                        const vector<KeyFrame*> vpMapKFs = pCurrentMap->GetAllKeyFrames();
+                        if(!vpMapKFs.empty())
+                            mCurrentFrame.SetNewBias((*max_element(vpMapKFs.begin(),vpMapKFs.end(),KeyFrame::lId))->GetImuBias());
+                    }
                     bOK = Relocalization();
                     if (bOK) { 
                         cout << "INIT_RELOCALIZE success!" << endl;
